<title>USA: Triumph Group boosts IPO to 2.5 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Triumph Group boosts IPO to 2.5 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triumph Group Inc, in a regulatory filing on Wednesday, raised to 2.5 million the number of shares it will offer in its planned initial public offering. The pricing range remains $16 to $18 a share.</p>
<p>The aircraft component maker had previously planned to offer 2.375 million shares, to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol &quot;TGI.&quot;</p>
<p>Alex Brown &amp; Sons Inc, the lead manager of the deal, said the company is tentatively scheduled to go public during the week of October 21.</p>
